.TH S3M-DIFF 1 "" "s3m @VERSION@" "s3m Manual"
.SH NAME
s3m\-diff \- parallel bucket and prefix comparison
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3m\-diff
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fILEFT\fR \fIRIGHT\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares two sides in parallel and reports every difference as CSV, ending with a summary and a plain-language verdict.
Each side is an \fBs3://BUCKET[/PREFIX]\fR URI or a local directory (both local is refused; use p3m\-diff).
Read-only: nothing on either side is modified.
.PP
By default keys, sizes and conclusive etags are compared.
Single-part uploads have the content MD5 as their etag, so equality there is content verification.
Local files have no etag, so a local-versus-S3 run compares keys and sizes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-checksum
Verify contents where the cheap checks are inconclusive: a local MD5 against a conclusive etag where possible (no network I/O), otherwise chunked reads or ranged GETs that stop at the first differing byte and report its offset.
Sizes gate everything: size-mismatched objects are never read.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " N"
Worker threads, 1\-256 (default 16).
.TP
.BI \-\-shard\-depth " N"
Prefix levels expanded for parallelism, 0\-9 (default 2).
.TP
.B \-\-rrdns
Resolve the endpoint hostname to every A/AAAA address and spread worker threads across them, moving a thread to the next address if its current one fails.
See
.BR s3m (7).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Write the CSV to FILE and show live progress.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the listing; the summary and verdict still print, making this a fast "are these the same?" check.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
The connection options \fB\-\-endpoint\fR, \fB\-\-region\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR, \fB\-\-path\-style\fR, \fB\-\-no\-sign\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR and \fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR are common to all s3m tools and are described in
.BR s3m (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No differences.
.TP
.B 1
Differences found.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or the comparison hit errors (the verdict is withheld because coverage was incomplete).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3m (7)
.BR s3m\-sync (1)
